Dijkstra's Algorithm

Dijkstra's Algorithm is a graph algorithm used to find the shortest path from one source vertex to all other vertices in a weighted graph.

Key Point

Dijkstra works when:

The graph is weighted
Edge weights are non-negative (weight >= 0)
It can work with directed or undirected graphs





How Dijkstra Works
Set the source distance to 0.
Set the distance of all other vertices to infinity.
Select the unvisited vertex having the smallest distance.
Visit its neighboring vertices.
Update their distances if a shorter path is found.
Mark the current vertex as visited.
Repeat until all vertices are processed.



